given-names></name><name><surname>Pirounaki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Papatsibas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Kontou-Kastellanou</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Moulakakis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical significance of serum procalcitonin levels in patients with acute or chronic liver disease</article-title><source>Eur J Gastroenterol Hepatol</source><year>2006</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>525</fpage><lpage>530</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16607149</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00042737-200605000-00012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Connert</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Stremmel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Elsin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Procalcitonin is a valid marker of infection in decompensated cirrhosis</article-title><source>Z Gastroenterol</source><year>2003</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12592597</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2003-37314</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bota</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Nuffelen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zakariah</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Serum levels of C-reactive protein and procalcitonin in critically ill patients with cirrhosis of the liver</article-title><source>J Lab Clin Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>146</volume><fpage>347</fpage><lpage>351</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16310518</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-